ence to work out the difference  being the righteous hero of the years i  doubt genus would be cool with killing  an innocent person in his place  so i think it's possible they did the  following instead  at this time hawks was not being  monitored by the villains alright this  was before  a skeptic put in all those cameras and  everything so hortz could do whatever he  wanted  and as illustrated by this handy diagram  top heroes have an extensive reach when  it comes to the hero commission  therefore he was still free to contact  the hero commission  and tell them of the current situation  my working theory  right now is that by pulling some  strings the hero commission were able to  acquire a body of a recently deceased  person  that has a similar stature to best genus  at which point  genus used his excellent set of skills  to give that person  a makeover so they resembled him as much  as humanly possible  that way no one was actually killed to  fulfill the mission  and the only real sacrifice was that the  number three hero  had to postpone his return to hero  activities  regarding why hawks took out the feather  sword in this moment is pretty  understandable when you look at the  whole situation  the fact remains that in this moment we  now know that hawks must have told genus  about the plan to kill another hero  and he doesn't know how best genius is  going to react in another reality  genus could have restrained hawkes right  there and then and also maybe he could  have been like no  like i want to return as a hero i'm not  going to hide away for several months  until you finish your plan  you know there's a lot of different  reasons why genus would have declined  the offer  and things could have turned ugly it was  only because of his resolve  that the mission was able to progress  the way it did but on the flip side  genius could have just as easily  declined and then who knows what could  have happened  it's highly likely that he pulled out  this sword fo